/// The theme contract, [[Theme]]. Implementations are sibling modules;
/// `theme-beer.pkl` (BeerCSS, Material 3) is the default.
///
/// A theme is any module exporting `theme: Theme`, for instance one in your
/// workspace beside `site.pkl`. An entry picks it with
/// `theme = import("theme-mine.pkl").theme` — the call form, since
/// `(import "x").theme` does not parse — and may amend it. Every property has a
/// working default, so `new Theme {}` is a whole theme: the HA tokens, no
/// framework, the bare frame.
///
/// ## A theme is the third CSS layer (ADR 0020)
///
///   1. `core/css.pkl` — the `fh-` layout contract, the `--fh-*` colour
///      variables, the runtime's own classes. Always there.
///   2. each card's `cardDef.css` — the structure of its markup.
///   3. the theme's `styles` — the palette, the `--fh-*` re-pointing, the
///      framework's own classes, and any retune of 1–2.
///
/// All three are one `<style>`, in that order, so the theme overrides by
/// cascade without restating anything.
///
/// ## What a card guarantees you
///
/// The classes your `styles` may restyle: `.fh-grid`/`.fh-row`/`.fh-col`, the
/// node wrapper `.fh-cell`, a query set's `.fh-group` (always a passthrough),
/// `.fh-cols-<1..12>`/`.fh-cols-full`, `.fh-start`, `.card`, `.fh-section`, a
/// labelled button's `.fh-press`, a tile's `.fh-tile` row, the shared glyph `.fh-badge`
/// and the `.fh-lines` text column,
/// `.fh-reading`, `.fh-sub`, `.popup`/`.popup-close`, `.tabs`/`.tabbar`/`.tab`,
/// `.entity-info`/`.entity-info-id`/`.entity-info-attrs`, and the slider's
/// `.slider-card`/`.slider-head`/`.slider-icon`/`.slider-actions`/
/// `.slider-body`/`.slider-members`/`.slider-group`.
///
/// A guarded action in flight puts `.fh-disabled` (inert) and `.fh-loading`
/// (still working) on the tapped element; a press the entity's state refuses
/// gets `.fh-disabled` alone. Both are immediate — they are the answer to the
/// tap — so keep them so. A failed action shows `.fh-toast`.
///
/// ## Your own class names in card markup
///
/// CSS cannot make one class inherit another's rules, so a framework class a
/// card should carry comes through [[classes]]: each `fh-` class you name, and
/// the classes the markup carries in its place. Keep the `fh-` class in the
/// content to add to it; leave it out to replace it, which also drops the base
/// CSS for it. The server applies this to every card's `class="…"` and
/// `data-class:…` and to the `.fh-cell` wrapper's classes, live ones included;
/// `fh-cell` and `fh-group` must stay in their own content.
///
///     classes {
///       ["fh-busy-spin"] = "shape loading-indicator"   // in its place
///       ["fh-disabled"]  = "fh-disabled disabled"      // beside it
///     }
///
/// The delayed spinner is the case that needs it. Style it as "showing", with
/// no delay of its own; the delay is already in the signal. `""` declines it.
/// A button's `fh-size-small`/`-medium`/`-large` are the other: map them to the
/// framework's own sizes, or set `--fh-press-size` on `.fh-press`.
///
/// ## Writing one
///
///   1. A module importing `@fh-dashboard/theme.pkl` and exporting
///      `theme: Theme`, or an `open class` extending it for amendable knobs.
///   2. `tokens`/`tokensDark`: HA-named tokens (`tokens.pkl` is the default),
///      emitted as `:root` properties; every `--fh-*` falls back to them.
///   3. `stylesheets`/`scripts`: pinned CDN links, never `@latest`. Ship JS
///      only for visuals your CSS needs, bound to survive morphs (delegated
///      listeners do); behaviour stays Datastar's. `inlineScripts` is the same
///      for JS you write yourself; a card's own script is the card's
///      (`cardDef.script`). Scripts reload the page when they change; `styles`
///      patches.
///   4. `styles`: the palette, the `--fh-*` re-pointing, your framework's
///      classes. A chart is drawn on the server, so it takes the theme only
///      through `--fh-chart-line` (else `--fh-accent`), `--fh-chart-fill`
///      (else none), `--fh-chart-grid` (else `--fh-border`) and
///      `--fh-chart-label` (else `--fh-text-dim`).
///   5. `classes`: see above.
///   6. `chrome`: the frame. It must wrap `{{{body}}}` in `id="dashboard"`
///      (checked by `Dashboard.validate`) and should host
///      `<div id="popups">{{{popups}}}</div>`, where a restored popup is baked
///      for the first paint; without it a popup still works, a moment late.
module theme

import "tokens.pkl" as tokenPalette

open class Theme {
  /// HA-named tokens, emitted as `:root` properties; every `--fh-*` variable
  /// falls back to them.
  tokens: Mapping<String, String> = tokenPalette.light
  /// The tokens that differ under `prefers-color-scheme: dark`.
  tokensDark: Mapping<String, String> = tokenPalette.dark
  stylesheets: Listing<String> = new {}
  /// Loaded off the critical path, so only for a sheet whose absence leaves the
  /// layout intact (an icon font). A text font stays in [[stylesheets]]:
  /// swapping it mid-paint moves every line.
  deferredStylesheets: Listing<String> = new {}
  /// ES module URLs, run after first paint.
  scripts: Listing<String> = new {}
  /// Classic scripts inlined in the head, run before first paint, after every
  /// card's `cardDef.script`.
  inlineScripts: Listing<String> = new {}
  styles: String = ""
  /// The page frame; the default is exactly the two hosts.
  chrome: String = """
    <main id="dashboard">{{{body}}}</main>
    <div id="popups">{{{popups}}}</div>
    """
  /// `fh-` class -> the space-separated classes in its place. See "Your own
  /// class names in card markup" above.
  classes: Mapping<String(startsWith("fh-")), String(matches(Regex(#"[\w -]*"#)))> = new {}
}
